# TBCC CC paste bridge (always on)

The operator **blind-pastes** Cursor completions into Claude Code (and the reverse) during multiphase CC Relay work. They do **not** want to read ACK prose between hops. Write every relay turn so the copy-paste is the product.

## Operator habit (locked)

- Cursor → Claude Code: whole reply or the fenced block gets pasted as-is.
- Claude Code → Cursor: same — often just the reverse report path + `/cc-report`, or a `PASTE INTO CURSOR` fence.
- Do **not** rely on “ACK stays in Cursor / don’t paste into CC.” That rule is retired.

## When this fires

- `/cc-report`, `/cc-run`, `/directive`, `/handoff-cc`, multiphase handoff ACK/STOP
- Any reply that tells Claude Code to start Phase N+1, amend, stop, or fix
- Any Claude Code phase completion meant to come back to Cursor

Skip for pure operator Q&A with no other-agent hop (still keep plain language).

## Cursor reply shape (required on relay turns)

1. **One short plain line** for the human (what happened / what to do) — plain-language rule still applies here.
2. **One fenced block** whose first line is exactly `PASTE INTO CLAUDE CODE` (or `PASTE INTO CLAUDE CODE — <short tag>`).
3. Inside the fence, address **Claude Code**, not the operator:
   - `Verdict:` ACK | fix | wait
   - `Report:` path under `tbcc/docs/handoffs/`
   - `Do:` exact next actions (phase, amend plan, stop conditions)
   - `Do not:` push / start bots / touch `.env` / Phase N+1 unless listed
4. Optional second fence only if Cursor also needs a human Tray smoke list — keep it after the paste fence, labeled clearly.

Do **not** make the human-facing ACK the only payload. If they paste the whole message, the fence must still be unambiguous.

### Template

````markdown
Topic wiring looks good.

```text
PASTE INTO CLAUDE CODE
Verdict: ACK — go Phase 3
Report: tbcc/docs/handoffs/YYYY-MM-DD_<topic>_report.md
Do: Execute Phase 3 only. Append reverse report. STOP for Cursor /cc-report.
Do not: push; start bots; apply island migration unless Do says so.
```
````

## Claude Code reply shape (required on relay turns)

After each phase (or when a pasted Cursor ACK arrives):

1. Do the work / honor the ACK.
2. Write/append `*_report.md`.
3. End with a fence whose first line is `PASTE INTO CURSOR`.
4. Inside: `/cc-report`, report path, phase status, HEAD hash if committed, one-line risks.

Treat a pasted `PASTE INTO CLAUDE CODE` fence as the **go signal** — same authority as disk `CURRENT_DIRECTIVE.md` for the named next step. Prefer the fence’s `Do:` over chat vibes when they conflict.

## Anti-patterns

- Long “for your eyes only” ACKs with no paste fence
- “Tell Claude to…” without a copy-ready block
- Asking the operator to summarize between tools
- Starting Phase N+1 from an ACK that said wait/fix
